// A bytes[] holds bytes buffers, so a literal handed a list type hands each of
// its own elements the element type, however deep the nesting goes: the rows of
// a bytes[] literal, the value of `rows[i] = [..]`, the argument of
// `push(rows, [..])`. Recomputed from the store alone, like every other mark,
// so a build that skips the type check answers the same as one that ran it.

